-- title:
--   Integrality of the base change X_O of the Γ_H(M) model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, that $M/p$ is nonzero, and that $H$ contains every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Let `hj` witness that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` — namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series with the integral $j$-numerator coefficients — lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios at full level. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, the bundle of properties of the two-chart model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over `R p`: properness, flatness and local finite presentation of the structure morphism, integrality and normality of all affine charts, properness and smoothness at level `ΓN`, a smooth proper curve model `Meta` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with an isomorphism onto the base change, Galois equivariance of its closed points, a chart-level identification of $q$-expansions, and smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : \mathrm{R}\,p \to A$ a ring homomorphism compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain) whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, and $\rho_O : \mathrm{R}\,p \to O$ any ring homomorphism. Then the base change `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, the fibre product of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` with $\mathrm{Spec}\,\rho_O$, is an integral scheme.
--
--   This is the integrality of the Deligne–Rapoport style integral model of $X_H(M)$ after base change to an unramified discrete valuation ring in which $p$ is a uniformiser; it is obtained from flatness, which makes $p$ a non-zero-divisor on every affine chart, together with integrality of the generic fibre on the basic open $\{p \neq 0\}$. It underlies the later analysis of the special fibre of this model, in particular the statements about branch ideals at the two charts, the germ of $p$ in the local rings and the Krull dimension of its stalks.
